The data structure used is an array, which provides fast insertion and deletion operations but may waste memory when the capacity is not reached. The linked list data structure can also be used to avoid this problem but requires more memory for each element.

In conclusion, this solution uses an array as the data structure because it provides fast insertion and deletion operations and ensures a fixed memory usage. However, if the input exceeds the array capacity, the function reallocates the memory to double the capacity, which may waste memory. Therefore, using a linked list data structure can help to avoid this problem while providing better performance for read and write operations.']

