The implementation also includes a caching mechanism using a `Map` object to store processed file contents for future requests. This helps to minimize memory usage by reusing already processed file contents instead of reading them from disk again. The `cache` map is populated with the results of processing each file, and subsequent requests for the same file can retrieve the cached content instead of re-processing it.

