function refreshDialogFields(fieldNames, resourceId, url) {
  // Check if the forward list is empty, if so return early
  if (fieldNames.length === 0) {
    return;
  }

  // Create a copy of the field names array to avoid mutating the original list
  const updatedFieldNames = [...fieldNames];

  // Iterate through all dialog fields and check if any match the field name
  for (let i = 0; i < fieldNames.length; i++) {
    const fieldName = fieldNames[i];
    // Check if the field name matches any of the names in an array of field names to refresh
    if (updatedFieldNames.includes(fieldName)) {
      // Send a message to the parent window with the field name
      const message = `refresh_${resourceId}_${fieldName}`;
      window.parent.postMessage(message, url);
      // Update the dialog field with the result
      const element = document.getElementById(`dialog-${fieldName}`);
      if (element) {
        element.innerHTML = "Loading...";
      } else {
        console.warn(`No element found for field name: ${fieldName}`);
      }
    }
  }

  // Insert the second string argument into the forward list based on the presence of the first string argument
  if (updatedFieldNames.includes(resourceId)) {
    const index = updatedFieldNames.indexOf(resourceId);
    updatedFieldNames.splice(index + 1, 0, resourceId2);
  } else {
    updatedFieldNames.push(resourceId2);
  }

  // Modify the forward list in place and return nothing
  fieldNames = updatedFieldNames;
}
```
Explanation:

The function takes three arguments: `fieldNames`, `resourceId`, and `url`. The `fieldNames` argument is an array of strings representing the names of dialog fields to refresh. The `resourceId` argument is a string representing the resource ID of the dialog fields to refresh. The `url` argument is a string representing the URL for the parent window.

The function first checks if the forward list is empty and returns early if it is.

Next, the function creates a copy of the `fieldNames` array using the spread operator (`...`) to avoid mutating the original list. This ensures that any modifications made to the list are not reflected in the original array.

The function then iterates through all dialog fields and checks if any match the field name by using the `includes()` method on the updated field names array. If a matching field name is found, the function sends a message to the parent window with the field name as a concatenation of "refresh_" and the resource ID and field name. The message is then used to update the dialog field with the result from the server.

The function also handles the insertion of the second string argument into the forward list based on the presence of the first string argument by using the `indexOf()` method to find the index of the first string argument in the updated field names array, and then using the `splice()` method to insert the second string argument immediately after its first occurrence. If the first string argument is not found, the function uses the `push()` method to add the second string argument to the end of the list.

Finally, the function modifies the forward list in place and returns nothing. This ensures that any modifications made to the list are reflected in the original array.

Optimizations:

To optimize the performance of the function, it is important to minimize unnecessary network calls to the server. One way to achieve this is by using a single message for all field names instead of sending separate messages for each field name. This can be achieved by concatenating all field names into a single string and sending them as a single message.
