```
class CombatEngine {
public:
    // Constructor
    CombatEngine(GameState* gameState) : gameState_(gameState) {}

    // Function to execute a combat action
    void ExecuteAction(Player* player, ActionType type, float value) {
        // Check if the player is still alive
        if (!player->IsAlive()) {
            return;
        }

        // Get the attack data for the given type
        AttackData attack = GetAttackData(type);

        // Calculate the attack damage and apply it to the target
        float damage = CalculateDamage(player, attack);
        player->GetTarget()->TakeDamage(damage);

        // Update the combat log with the attack information
        CombatLogEntry entry;
        entry.timestamp = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();
        entry.attacker = player;
        entry.target = player->GetTarget();
        entry.damage = damage;
        gameState_->AddCombatLogEntry(entry);
    }

private:
    // Get the attack data for a given type
    AttackData GetAttackData(ActionType type) {
        switch (type) {
            case ActionType::MELEE:
                return MeleeAttack;
            case ActionType::RANGED:
                return RangedAttack;
            case ActionType::MAGIC:
                return MagicAttack;
            default:
                return AttackData();
        }
    }

    // Calculate the damage dealt by an attack
    float CalculateDamage(Player* player, const AttackData& attack) {
        float baseDamage = attack.baseDamage;
        float bonusDamage = 0;

        if (player->HasBuff("Attack Boost")) {
            bonusDamage += attack.bonusDamage * player->GetBuffValue("Attack Boost");
        }

        return baseDamage + bonusDamage;
    }

    // The game state object
    GameState* gameState_;
};
```
This class contains a number of private and public methods that allow it to manage combat actions. The `ExecuteAction` method is the main entry point for executing a combat action, and it takes care of things like checking if the player is still alive, calculating the attack damage, and updating the game state with information about the attack.

The `GetAttackData` method retrieves the attack data for a given type, which includes the base damage and any bonus damage that may be applied. The `CalculateDamage` method takes into account any active buffs that may affect the player's attack power.

This class also contains a number of private fields that are used to manage the game state, such as the `gameState_` object. These fields are initialized in the constructor and used throughout the class to keep track of information about the game state.

To use this class, you would need to create an instance of it and then call the `ExecuteAction` method whenever a player performs a combat action. For example:
