Here is a possible implementation of the JavaScript function that dynamically refreshes specified dialog fields in an AngularJS application:
```
function refreshDialogFields(resourceIds, urls) {
  const promises = [];

  // Iterate over the list of resource IDs and URLs
  for (let i = 0; i < resourceIds.length; i++) {
    const id = resourceIds[i];
    const url = urls[i];

    // Create a promise to fetch the data from the URL
    promises.push(fetch(url).then((response) => response.json()));
  }

  // Wait for all promises to resolve and then refresh the dialog fields
  Promise.all(promises).then((responses) => {
    const data = responses.map((response) => response.data);

    // Refresh the dialog fields with the new data
    for (let i = 0; i < resourceIds.length; i++) {
      const id = resourceIds[i];
      const field = document.getElementById(id);
      if (field) {
        field.value = data[i];
      }
    }
  });
}
```
This function takes two arguments: `resourceIds` and `urls`, which are arrays of strings representing the IDs and URLs of the resources to be fetched, respectively. It then creates an array of promises using the `fetch()` method to fetch the data from each URL in parallel. Once all the promises have resolved, it waits for them to complete and then refreshes the dialog fields with the new data by setting their values to the corresponding elements in the `data` array.

