using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Runtime.Serialization.Formatters.Binary;

public class CustomDataStructure {
  public string Id { get; set; }
  public string Name { get; set; }
}

public static CustomDataStructure[] LoadCustomData(string fileName) {
  // Use the BinaryFormatter to deserialize the data from the file
  using (var stream = File.OpenRead(fileName)) {
    var formatter = new BinaryFormatter();
    return (CustomDataStructure[])formatter.Deserialize(stream);
  }
}
```
This function takes a single argument: `fileName`, which is the name of the binary file to be loaded. It uses the `BinaryFormatter` class to deserialize the data from the file into an array of `CustomDataStructure` objects.

To integrate these functions seamlessly, you can use a third function that calls both `refreshDialogFields()` and `LoadCustomData()` in parallel:
```
public void RefreshDialogFieldsAndLoadData(string[] resourceIds, string[] urls) {
  // Call refreshDialogFields() to update the dialog fields
  refreshDialogFields(resourceIds, urls);

  // Use a Task.WhenAll() to wait for both functions to complete
  Task.WhenAll(refreshDialogFields(resourceIds, urls), LoadCustomData("custom_data.bin"))).ContinueWith((t) => {
    // Update the data structure with the new data from LoadCustomData()
    var customData = t.Result;
    for (int i = 0; i < resourceIds.Length; i++) {
      string id = resourceIds[i];
      CustomDataStructure data = customData.FirstOrDefault(x => x.Id == id);
      if (data != null) {
        // Update the dialog field with the new data from LoadCustomData()
        document.getElementById(id).value = data.Name;
      }
    }
  });
}
```
This function takes two arguments: `resourceIds` and `urls`, which are arrays of strings representing the IDs and URLs of the resources to be fetched, respectively. It first calls `refreshDialogFields()` to update the dialog fields with the new data from the server. Then it uses `Task.WhenAll()` to wait for both functions to complete in parallel. Once both functions have completed, it updates the data structure with the new data from `LoadCustomData()` and updates the dialog fields with the new data using the `document.getElementById()` method.

