    records[i].offset = i * sizeof(long); // Replace with desired offset value
}

// Batch the accesses to the records into groups of `BATCH_SIZE`
#define BATCH_SIZE 32
for (int i = 0; i < num_records; i += BATCH_SIZE) {
    // Prefetch the next batch of records
    for (int j = i + BATCH_SIZE; j < num_records && j < i + 2 * BATCH_SIZE; j++) {
        __builtin_prefetch(&records[j], 0, 3);
    }

    // Access the records in the batch
    for (int j = i; j < i + BATCH_SIZE; j++) {
        // Access the record
        records[j].key;
        records[j].offset;
    }
}
```
Note that this code will prefetch the next batch of records and access them in parallel with the previous batch. This can improve cache performance, but it is important to choose an appropriate value for `BATCH_SIZE` that balances performance and memory usage.

6. To handle a large number of keys efficiently, we can use techniques such as data compression and hashing. For example, we can compress the key values using LZ77 or Huffman coding:
```c
const int KEY_LENGTH = 10; // Replace with desired length of keys
int num_keys = 100000; // Replace with desired number of keys
int* keys = (int*) malloc(sizeof(int) * num_keys);
for (int i = 0; i < num_keys; i++) {
    keys[i] = generate_key(KEY_LENGTH); // Generate a random key value
}

// Compress the keys using LZ77 or Huffman coding
#include <lz77.h>
int* compressed_keys = (int*) malloc(sizeof(int) * num_keys);
for (int i = 0; i < num_keys; i++) {
    int len = sizeof(int);
    char* buf = (char*) &keys[i];
    char* comp = lz77_compress(buf, len);
    compressed_keys[i] = *((int*) comp);
}
```
Note that this code will compress the keys using LZ77 compression. This can reduce the memory usage and improve performance when accessing the keys. However, it is important to choose an appropriate value for `KEY_LENGTH` that balances performance and memory usage.

In summary, the key to handling a large number of records efficiently in C++ is to use techniques such as data alignment, cache optimization, and data compression to minimize memory usage and improve performance. It is also important to choose an appropriate value for `BATCH_SIZE` that balances performance and memory usage when accessing the records in batches.']

