* Fault tolerance: Implement redundancy in the microservices architecture by deploying multiple instances of each service. This ensures that if one instance fails, traffic can be directed to other instances to minimize downtime.
* Service degradation: Use a circuit breaker pattern to detect and mitigate service failures. When a service is detected as failing, the circuit breaker will redirect traffic to other services until the failure has been resolved.

