The `initNetworkInterfaceList` function initializes the head node of the linked list and adds a new node for each interface to the linked list. It then initializes the data fields for each interface using random values.

The `updateNetworkInterfaceList` function updates the data for each network interface in the linked list by incrementing the packet loss rate, updating the throughput and latency, and moving to the next node in the linked list.

The `cleanupNetworkInterfaceList` function clears and frees the memory allocated for the linked list when it is no longer needed by looping through each node in the linked list and freeing its memory. It then frees the head node of the linked list.']

